<title>POLAND: Poland and EU finish statistics reform programme.</title>
<headline>Poland and EU finish statistics reform programme.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Central Statistical Office (GUS) and the European Union (EU) have ended a two-year programme, worth some 12.3 million Ecu, aimed at upgrading Polish statistics, GUS said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>GUS said the programme mapped out the development of Polish statistics for the next five years and modernised the country's statistical infrastructure.</p>
<p>It said the programme, called POLSTAT, also helped Poland bring its classification procedures in line with those in the EU, which it intends to join.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
